---
import Layout from "@/layouts/Layout.astro";
import Image from "astro/components/Image.astro";

import venmo_qr_code from "@assets/venmo_qr_code.png";
import sponsor_tiers from "@assets/sponsor_tiers.png";
import SponsorGrid from "@/components/SponsorGrid.astro";
---

<Layout title="Support Us" description="" selected="donate" footerless>
  <section id="top-content" class="oswald-text">
    <div id="top-content-header">
      <h1>Supporting FRC Team 6324</h1>
      <p>
        Our sponsors and community partners make everything we do possible.
        Their generosity and support allow our team to learn, compete, travel,
        and create opportunities that inspire the next generation of leaders. We
        are incredibly grateful for their investment in our team and our
        mission, and we are proud to recognize the organizations and individuals
        that help make these experiences possible
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section id="supporting" class="oswald-text">
    <ul id="support-methods">
      <li>
        <h2>Materials</h2>
        <p>
          Material costs are one of our largest expenses each year. In producing
          a high-quality robot, we typically use thousands of dollars in
          aluminum, structural plastics, fasteners, and electronics. Directly
          supplying these materials via in-kind donations helps us reduce our
          annual supply budget.
        </p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <h2>Monetary</h2>
        <p>
          Monetary donations are the most flexible way of supporting our
          program. We give our sponsors the choice to divert funds to a specific
          aspect of our budget including, but not limited to, registration
          costs, build budget, travel expenses, and apparel. Every dollar helps
          reduce the cost to our students.
        </p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <h2>Mentoring</h2>
        <p>
          Become a mentor! We are always looking for professionals interested in
          working directly with our students either in-person at our meetings or
          at job sites through internships. We are actively recruiting mentors
          for business, CAD, manufacturing, media, outreach, software
          development, and more! To become a mentor or provide an opportunity
          for our students, please contact one of <a href="mailto:frc6324.leadmentor@gmail.com">our Lead Mentors</a>.
        </p>
      </li>
    </ul>
    <div id="support-sidebar">
      <div id="venmo-qr-code">
        <Image
          src={venmo_qr_code}
          alt=""
          layout="full-width"
          inferSize={true}
          priority={true}
        />
      </div>
      <p>
        The easiest way to support us is to send us money via Venmo! Scan the qr
        code above or go to <a href="">this Venmo page</a> to easily support Salem
        Robotics.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
  <hr style="width: 100%; height: 5px; background-color: var(--text);" />
  <section id="sponsorship-container" class="oswald-text">
    <div id="sponsorship">
      <h2>Sponsorship</h2>
      <p>
        Sponsorship is the best way to support our team. we rely on our sponsors
        to help with the high cost of participation associated with FIRST
        Robotics Competition and our community outreach programs. Our community
        partners are critical to our efforts in making sure that all students
        can participate in our programs and grow as professionals, regardless of
        their economic status.
      </p>
      <h3>Investing in Your Future</h3>
      <p>
        Our program is at the forefront of helping our students develop the
        technical and professional skills that they need to succeed in their
        future professions and their lives overall after high school. You can
        directly support our efforts in preparing the next generation of
        engineers and technical experts.
      </p>
      <p>
        Of our graduates, over &frac23; stay local, pursuing educational
        opportunities and careers in the New Hampshire and greater New England
        area. Of that group, nearly all students that have pursued an internship
        with one of our sponsors while they were in high school have continued
        working their post graduation. By supporting our program you are not
        only supporting students in your community, you are also supporting your
        future workforce and ensuring that these students will have the skills
        that you and your clients are looking for.
      </p>
      <h3>Benefits</h3>
      <p>
        Beyond supporting the next generation of engineers, scientists, and
        business professionals, sponsors also receive many benefits depending on
        the donation level. These include, but are <em>not</em> limited to:
      </p>
      <ul id="sponsor-benefits">
        <li>
          Exposure via our:
          <ul>
            <li>website</li>
            <li>T-shirts</li>
            <li>pit banners</li>
            <li>robots</li>
            <li>technical binders</li>
            <li>any other promotional material we produce</li>
          </ul>
        </li>
        <li>The ability to request robot demos at your place of business.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
    <div id="sponsor-sidebar">
      <h3>Sponsor Tiers:</h3>
      <Image
        src={sponsor_tiers}
        alt=""
        layout="full-width"
        id="sponsor-tier-image"
      />
    </div>
  </section>
  <div class="no-print">
    <SponsorGrid />
  </div>
  <section id="nonprofit-info" class="oswald-text">
    <div id="nonprofit-contacts">
      <h3>Contacts</h3>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <p class="contact-name">John Seeman</p>
          <p class="contact-position">Lead Mentor</p>
          <a href="mailto:frc6324.leadmentor@gmail.com" class="contact-email"
            >frc6324.leadmentor@gmail.com</a
          >
        </li>
        <li class="vertical-line"></li>
        <li>
          <p class="contact-name">Heather Dezan</p>
          <p class="contact-position">President, Friends of SHS Robotics</p>
          <a href="mailto:friendsofshsrobotics@gmail.com" class="contact-email"
            ><p>friendsofshsrobotics@gmail.com</p></a
          >
        </li>
        <li class="vertical-line"></li>
        <li>
          <p class="contact-name">Brennan Macaig</p>
          <p class="contact-position">Treasurer, Friends of SHS Robotics</p>
          <a href="mailto:brennan.macaig@gmail.com" class="contact-email"
            ><p>brennan.macaig@gmail.com</p></a
          >
        </li>
      </ul>
    </div>
    <div id="nonprofit-info-and-mail">
      <div id="nonprofit-info-disclaimer">
        <h3>Nonprofit Info</h3>
        <style>
          .inline-block {
            display: inline-block;
          }
        </style>
        <p>
          Team 6324, The Blue Devils, maintains non-profit status through the <span
            class="inline-block">Salem School District (SAU 57);</span
          >
          <span class="inline-block">Tax ID 02-6000816</span> and the <span
            class="inline-block">501(c)(3)</span
          >
          charitable organization <span class="inline-block"
            >‘Friends of SHS Robotics’;
          </span>
          <span class="inline-block">Tax ID 93-4339616.</span>
          A <span class="inline-block">W-9</span> Taxpayer Identification Certificate
          can be provided for either entity upon request. Both in-kind and monetary
          donations are accepted and are typically tax deductible. Checks can be made
          payable to ‘Friends of SHS Robotics’ with ‘FRC Team 6324’ in the memo line.
          Donations made after February 1st of each year will be attributed to the
          following competitive season (January-April timeframe) and rewards will
          be granted before the end of June of the applicable season.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div id="nonprofit-mail">
        <h3>Mailing Address</h3>
        <div>
          <p>Attn: FIRST Robotics</p>
          <p>CTE Department</p>
          <p>Salem High School</p>
          <p>44 Geremonty Drive,</p>
          <p>Salem, New Hampshire 03079</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
  <style>
    #top-content {
      & #top-content-header {
        width: 100%;
        display: flex;
        flex-direction: column;
        align-items: center;

        & h1 {
          width: fit-content;
          font-size: 3rem;
          margin-block: 5rem;
        }

        & p {
          width: 80%;
          font-size: 1.5rem;
        }
      }
    }

    #supporting {
      display: flex;
      justify-content: space-between;
      height: fit-content;
    }

    #support-methods {
      list-style: none;
      width: 60vw;
      padding: 0;
      margin: 0 0 2.5rem;

      & li {
        width: 100%;
        display: flex;
        flex-direction: column;
        align-items: center;
      }

      & li h2 {
        font-size: 2rem;
      }

      & li p {
        width: 75%;
        margin: 0;
        font-size: 1.25rem;
      }
    }

    #support-sidebar {
      width: 40vw;
      display: flex;
      flex-direction: column;
      align-items: center;

      & p {
        width: 80%;
      }
    }

    #sponsorship-container {
      width: 100%;
      display: flex;
      flex-direction: row;
      align-items: center;

      & #sponsorship {
        width: 65vw;
        display: flex;
        flex-direction: column;
        align-items: center;
        font-size: 1.25rem;

        & h2 {
          font-size: 2.125rem;
        }

        & h3 {
          font-size: 1.5rem;
        }

        & p {
          width: 80%;
        }
      }
    }

    #sponsor-benefits {
      width: 75%;

      & > li > ul {
        padding-block: 10px;
        display: grid;
        grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr);
        gap: 1rem;
      }
    }

    #sponsor-sidebar {
      display: flex;
      flex-direction: column;
      align-items: center;
      font-size: 2rem;
      font-weight: bolder;

      & #sponsor-tier-image {
        width: 30vw;
        height: auto;
      }
    }

    #nonprofit-info {
      width: 100%;
    }

    #nonprofit-contacts {
      width: 100%;

      & > h3 {
        width: 100%;
        text-align: center;
        font-size: 2.5rem;
        font-weight: bolder;

        margin: 10px 0 10px;
      }

      & > ul {
        width: 100%;
        display: flex;
        flex-direction: row;
        list-style: none;
        justify-content: space-around;

        & > li :not(.vertical-line) {
          & .contact-name {
            font-size: 1.4rem;
          }

          & .contact-position {
            font-size: 1.2rem;
          }

          & .contact-email {
            color: var(--text);
          }

          width: 30vw;
        }
      }
    }

    #nonprofit-info-and-mail {
      width: 100%;
      display: flex;
      flex-direction: row-reverse;
      justify-content: space-around;

      & #nonprofit-info-disclaimer {
        width: 50vw;

        & > h3 {
          font-size: 2rem;
        }

        & > p {
          font-size: 1.25rem;
          font-weight: normal;
        }
      }

      & #nonprofit-mail {
        width: 30vw;
        display: flex;
        flex-direction: column;

        & > h3 {
          width: 100%;
          text-align: center;
          font-size: 1.8rem;
        }
      }
    }
  </style>
</Layout>
